#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hee4db — agent-first CLI over hee4-ops.db, the HEE v4 planning/ops database.

Not the engine ledger (K1 hee4-core::store owns that, ULTRAMAP §5a). Read-only by default; writes go
through named verbs only, one transaction each. Python stdlib plus the tursodb 0.7.2 binary.

Exit codes (the roster contract): 0 ok · 10 ok-with-gaps · 20 refused / failed check · 30 unmeasured
· 2 usage · 3 setup. Every counting output carries measured=N/M; the last stderr line is the typed
verdict line `hee4db <verb> verdict=… exit=…`.

Engine roles (measured 2026-10-01 on tursodb 0.7.2, see README § Writer safety):
  * the ONE writer is Python sqlite3 (BEGIN IMMEDIATE, synchronous=FULL read back, rollback on error);
  * reads run on Python sqlite3 `mode=ro` + query_only + an authorizer that denies every non-read
    action, OR on `tursodb --readonly` one-shot (`--engine turso`), both bounded at acquisition;
  * tursodb is never opened read-write on the main file: a rw open locks Python readers out, and its
    stdin batches are not atomic;
  * full-text search runs on a derived Tantivy sidecar (hee4-ops-search.db, --experimental-index-method),
    queried on a private per-query copy because tursodb refuses fts_match under --readonly.
"""
